-- Keep the prompt-driven workflow concise and make learning capture a required action.
UPDATE skills
SET
  content = E'## Self-Improvement\n\nBefore your final reply, record one compact durable memory whenever you identify an explicit user correction, a verified non-obvious error, a missing capability request, or a better repeatable approach.\n\nUse one of these formats:\n- `[Learning: correction|knowledge_gap|best_practice] Area: <area>. Rule: <condition and required action>.`\n- `[Error] Area: <area>. Failure: <brief failure>. Cause: <verified cause>. Prevention: <specific action>.`\n- `[Feature Request] Capability: <request>. Need: <why it matters>. Suggested direction: <if known>.`\n\nSave only verified, reusable rules. Use `importance_score` 0.85–0.95 for corrections and significant errors, or 0.75–0.84 for other durable learnings. Do not save secrets, raw logs, transient state, routine retries, or unverified hypotheses. Do not claim a save unless the tool confirms it.\n\nPromote a pattern only after three independent verified occurrences, or when the user explicitly requests it. Check for duplicates first. Promote guidance or workflows with `native_create_skill`; promote only validated deterministic pure transformations with `native_create_code_tool`. Set promoted resources to `ephemeral=false`. Never automatically create HTTP tools.',
  updated_at = NOW()
WHERE workspace_id IS NULL AND name = 'Self-Improvement';
